# Without this, a Windows checkout (git's core.autocrlf=true default there)
# silently converts these to CRLF line endings, which breaks them in ways
# that don't announce themselves: a CRLF shebang line makes direct
# execution (`./script.sh`) fail with a confusing "No such file or
# directory" naming the interpreter-plus-\r, and a CRLF-terminated
# `set -euo pipefail` line fails with "pipefail: invalid option name" --
# found the hard way, verifying infra/helm/aiva and the Docker/compose
# changes in ADR-030 required actually running scripts/check_no_egress.sh,
# which wouldn't run at all on this checkout until this was fixed.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.conf.template text eol=lf
